{
  "summary": "Start by applying for your HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter, as it is required before you can submit a BTO application. Gather the necessary documents such as identity cards, income statements, and CPF contribution records to support the HFE application.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Apply for the HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter through the HDB portal; the letter confirms you meet the basic eligibility criteria for a first‑timer BTO.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Prepare the required documents for the HFE application, including NRICs, recent payslips or CPF contribution statements, and a declaration that neither applicant has previously owned a HDB flat or received a housing subsidy.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Check that both applicants are at least 21 years old and are Singapore Citizens, which you already meet.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Once the HFE letter is issued (valid for 6 months), you can proceed to register for the upcoming BTO launch and submit your application within the ballot period.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Exact document requirements and processing times may change; verify the latest checklist on the official HDB website (https://www.hdb.gov.sg) before submitting.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [
    {
      "field": "hfe_status",
      "needed_for": ["application_requirements"],
      "follow_up_question": "Have you already submitted an HFE application, and if so, what is its current status?"
    },
    {
      "field": "hfe_issue_date",
      "needed_for": ["application_timing"],
      "follow_up_question": "If you have received the HFE letter, on which date was it issued?"
    }
  ],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "With a valid HFE letter issued on 15 June 2026, you should ensure you apply before it expires (typically 2 years), gather the required documents, and be aware of the steps and deadlines in the sales launch.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "An HFE letter for first-timer couples is generally valid for 2 years from the issue date, provided there are no changes to the household composition.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Confirm the expiry date of your HFE letter (likely 15 June 2028) and ensure you submit your BTO application before that date.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Prepare the required documents for the application, including identity cards, marriage certificate, HFE letter, and recent income documents for the applicant(s).",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Check that both applicants meet the age requirement (at least 21 years old) and that the Singapore Citizen is the primary applicant, as required for first-timer couples.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Verify that neither applicant has previously owned a HDB flat or received a housing subsidy, as this would affect first-timer eligibility.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c6",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Review the sales launch timeline on the HDB website to know the ballot opening date, application submission window, and payment deadlines.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c7",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "If any change occurs in your household (e.g., change of citizenship, marriage status, or addition of a child) after the HFE letter is issued, you must inform HDB and may need a new HFE letter.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c8",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Keep copies of all documents and the HFE letter handy for the online application, as you will need to upload them to the HDB Flat Portal.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c9",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Exact expiry periods and document checklists can vary; please verify the latest details on the official HDB website (https://www.hdb.gov.sg) or the HDB Flat Portal (https://homes.hdb.gov.sg).",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "After completing the preliminary HFE check, you have up to 6 months to submit your full application (Step 2). Once HDB receives your complete application, processing typically takes about 4–6 weeks.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "The HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter issued after the preliminary check is valid for 6 months, within which you must submit your full BTO application (Step 2).",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "HDB usually takes 4 to 6 weeks to process a complete BTO application after it is submitted.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Processing times can vary depending on the volume of applications and any additional information HDB may request.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "You can apply for a BTO as an engaged couple who are both Singapore Citizens and first‑timers, provided you each meet the age requirement and other eligibility conditions.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "First‑timer couples (married or engaged) where both partners are Singapore Citizens and have never owned a flat or received a housing subsidy are eligible to apply for a BTO.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Each applicant must be at least 21 years old on the date of application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Obtain a HDB Flat Eligibility (HFE) letter for each applicant before the BTO ballot opens.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Gather required documents such as NRICs, income documents, and proof of citizenship for the HFE application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Exact dates for the next BTO launch and HFE letter validity periods can change; check the HDB website for the latest schedule.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [
    {
      "field": "applicant_1.age",
      "needed_for": ["application_requirements"],
      "follow_up_question": "How old is Rachel?"
    },
    {
      "field": "applicant_2.age",
      "needed_for": ["application_requirements"],
      "follow_up_question": "How old is Jun Hao?"
    }
  ],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "As a married couple where both partners are Singapore Citizens, have no prior HDB flat ownership or subsidies, you qualify as a first‑timer household. The household rules require at least one Singapore Citizen applicant, both applicants must be at least 21 years old, and you must not have owned any private residential property in the past 30 months.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "For a first‑timer household, at least one applicant must be a Singapore Citizen.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Both spouses must be at least 21 years old to apply for a BTO flat.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "A married couple where neither partner has previously owned an HDB flat or received any HDB housing subsidy is considered a first‑timer household.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "First‑timer households are not allowed to own any private residential property within the 30 months preceding the HFE application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "A married couple can have up to two applicants (both spouses) and up to four occupiers (including children, if any).",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c6",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Ensure both you and Leon have valid Singapore NRICs and are prepared to submit the HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter as part of the BTO application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c7",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Gather supporting documents such as NRICs, marriage certificate, and income statements for the HFE application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "Yes, owning a private residential property can affect your eligibility for a BTO as a first‑timer couple. You must not own any private residential property at the time of application, and the HFE letter will confirm this condition.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "First‑timer couples must not own any private residential property at the time of applying for a BTO.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "The HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter will state whether you meet the ownership condition and is required before you can submit a BTO application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "If you currently own a private residential property, you need to sell it and obtain the sale completion letter before applying for the HFE letter.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Specific details such as the exact timing of the sale and HFE issuance may vary; please verify the latest guidance on the HDB website (https://www.hdb.gov.sg).",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "Harith, being 20 years old, does not meet the minimum age of 21 required to be an HDB applicant, so he cannot be a joint applicant with you at this time.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "HDB requires each applicant to be at least 21 years old at the time of application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Age requirements are subject to change; please verify the current minimum age on the official HDB website.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Harith can wait until he turns 21, after which you both can apply together as joint applicants.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "In the meantime, you can each independently apply for an HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter once you meet the age requirement.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "Yes, Harith can be a joint applicant with you as both are Singapore Citizens, first‑timers, and meet the minimum age requirement of 21 years. Ensure you both obtain an HFE letter before applying.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "For a first‑timer couple, both partners must be Singapore Citizens or one Singapore Citizen and one Singapore Permanent Resident, and each must be at least 21 years old to be an applicant.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Engaged couples are allowed to apply together as joint applicants for a BTO flat.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Both Tan Li and Harith should apply for the HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter before submitting a BTO application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Eligibility is ultimately determined by HDB; this guidance does not guarantee approval.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "You should ensure your HFE letter is still valid and that any changes to your personal details or employment are updated before Step 2. Also confirm you have the required documents ready for the application.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Verify that your HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter, issued after completing Step 1, is still within its validity period before proceeding to Step 2.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Check that there have been no changes to your citizenship status, age, marital status, or employment that would affect eligibility, and update HDB if any changes occurred.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Gather the required documents for Step 2, such as NRICs, latest income documents, and the HFE letter, to upload when you submit the application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "If you are unsure about the exact validity period of your HFE letter or any document requirements, please refer to the official HDB website or the HDB Flat Portal for the latest information.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "You can apply for the HFE letter now; it is typically valid for one year, allowing you to wait for the October launch. Ensure you submit the HFE application promptly and keep the letter safe for the upcoming ballot.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "The HFE (HDB Flat Eligibility) letter is generally valid for one year from the date of issue.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Apply for the HFE letter now through the HDB e-Services portal to secure eligibility for the upcoming BTO launch.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Keep the HFE letter safe and ensure it remains valid when you submit your BTO application during the October ballot.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "If the HFE letter is issued close to the October launch, verify that its one‑year validity will still cover the application deadline; otherwise you may need to re‑apply.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "No, you do not need to be married to apply for a BTO; engaged couples can apply as long as both are Singapore Citizens and meet the other first‑timer requirements. You can submit your application now and register your marriage later if you wish.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "First‑timer couples can be either married or engaged; marriage registration is not a prerequisite for submitting a BTO application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Both applicants must be Singapore Citizens and at least 21 years old to be eligible as first‑timer applicants.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Prepare the required documents (e.g., NRICs, income documents, and the HFE letter) and submit your BTO application as an engaged couple.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "If you later decide to marry, you should update your marital status in HDB records, but this does not affect the already‑submitted BTO application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "No, you can apply now because at least one applicant (Nadia) is over 21; the 21‑year‑old rule applies to each individual applicant, not to the couple as a whole.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "For a first‑timer BTO application, each individual applicant must be at least 21 years old, but only one of the two applicants needs to meet the age requirement.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "If one applicant is 21 or older, the couple can submit a BTO application without waiting for the younger partner to turn 21.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Eligibility also depends on other criteria such as citizenship, prior flat ownership, and HFE letter status; please verify those details on the HDB website.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "To apply for your first BTO as an engaged Singapore‑citizen couple, you need to obtain an HFE letter, gather required documents (identification, income, employment, and marital status proof), and follow the pre‑application steps before the ballot opens.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Both partners must be Singapore Citizens or one Singapore Citizen and one Singapore Permanent Resident for a first‑timer BTO application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "At least one applicant must be 21 years old or older; both Mei (27) and you (28) meet the age requirement.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "As an engaged couple, you can apply as co‑applicants, with one designated as the primary applicant.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "First‑timer couples must not have previously owned any HDB flat or received any HDB subsidy.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Apply for a HDB Flat Eligibility (HFE) letter via the HDB portal; the letter is valid for 6 months from the issue date.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c6",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Prepare the following documents for the HFE application: NRICs, marriage/engagement certificate, latest payslips (last 3 months) or CPF contribution statements, and employment letters confirming your current occupations.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c7",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Check your HFE status once issued; you will need the HFE reference number when submitting the BTO ballot.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c8",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Monitor the HDB website for upcoming BTO project launch dates and ballot opening periods.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c9",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Create a HDB account on the HDB Flat Portal (https://homes.hdb.gov.sg) if you do not already have one, and link both applicants to the same household.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c10",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Exact document requirements and processing times may vary; please verify the latest checklist on the official HDB website.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "No, you cannot apply under the FT(PMC) category because one of you (Darren) has previously owned an HDB flat, which disqualifies you from the first-timer scheme.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "The FT(PMC) (First-Timer – Private Market Conversion) scheme is only open to couples where both applicants are first-time HDB flat buyers, meaning neither has ever owned a resale HDB flat or a subsidised flat before.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "A prior ownership of an HDB flat, even if it was sold later, makes the applicant ineligible for the FT(PMC) scheme.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Since Darren previously owned an HDB flat, you should consider applying under the regular First-Timer (FT) scheme or another appropriate scheme for non‑first‑timer couples.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Eligibility rules can be updated, so verify the latest criteria on the HDB website or the HDB Flat Portal before submitting your application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "Yes, both of you can be applicants for a first‑timer BTO as you are Singapore Citizens and over 21 years old.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "For a first‑timer BTO, each applicant must be a Singapore Citizen and at least 21 years old.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "A married or engaged couple can each be an applicant, provided they meet the citizenship and age requirements.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Proceed to apply jointly as co‑applicants when you submit your HFE (Flat Eligibility) application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "The Enhanced CPF Housing Grant amount depends on your household income and other factors, which requires a detailed calculation that is out of scope here. You should check the official HDB website or use the HDB calculator for the exact figure.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Calculating the exact Enhanced CPF Housing Grant amount is beyond the scope of this guidance.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": [
    {
      "code": "excluded_topic",
      "topic": "grant_loan_calculation",
      "detail": "User asked for the specific amount of the Enhanced CPF Housing Grant, which requires grant amount calculation.",
      "redirect_url": "https://www.hdb.gov.sg"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "We cannot estimate your chances of receiving a queue number for a 4‑room flat in Punggol. Instead, we can outline the steps you need to take to apply for a BTO as a first‑timer engaged couple.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Estimating the likelihood of obtaining a queue number for a specific BTO project is not possible without official HDB data and is outside the scope of this guidance.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "First‑timer couples (married or engaged) who are both Singapore Citizens are eligible to apply for a BTO flat, provided they meet the age and other basic eligibility criteria.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Both applicants must be at least 21 years old on the date of application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
